to many people fitness and performance  simply means being really strong or  maybe being able to run long distances  but this isn't fitness this is simply  being highly capable at a single task  this doesn't prepare you for all the  challenges life will throw at you and it  doesn't develop your body and mind in a  truly comprehensive and well-rounded  manner it won't undo the significant  damage caused by decades of sitting in  the chair mildly stressed it's time to  rethink what training can mean if you're  professional athletes then I fully  understand that sprinting lifting  weights swimming diving or another sport  is your career and your passion you have  a genuine shot at being the very best in  the world and therefore all your efforts  should be focused on that one thing but  for everyone else if the goal of  training is to improve quality of life  and physical and mental performance  specialization doesn't make any sense at  least not to me you tend to see this  most often with weightlifting people  obsess over their benchpress deadlift  and squat one rep maxes they push  themselves harder and harder further and  further why so they can be the best at  their gym or the best on an online forum  meanwhile they might completely ignore  their mobility or their ability to focus  for long periods nagging pains or their  endurance they even forget other aspects  of strength such as rotational strength  or straight arm strength there comes a  certain point where you see diminishing  returns  being able to benchpress a lot of weight  will have direct benefits on your daily  life and give you a sense of  accomplishment but does being able to  bench 150 kilograms instead of 140  kilograms have the same major benefits  why dedicate all of your efforts to that  one singular goal that tiny improvement  when so many other aspects of your  physical and mental performance could  benefit by being brought up to the same  level of course it's not just weight  lifters who fall foul of this  calisthenics athletes will often obsess  over their next skill without thinking  about endurance endurance athletes will  often run huge distances without  thinking what it's doing to their body  many other people will simply pick a  sport and focus on that be it dance bit  park or beach soccer some sports  inherently develop more well-rounded  individuals owing to a higher number of  techniques and various challenges dance  and martial arts come to mind but no  single activity will test you in  anything close to your full range of  abilities I'm not saying you shouldn't  aim to get better you should always  strive to be better if you  left 140 kilograms then absolutely you  should still aim for that hundred and  fifty but I'd rather be stronger than  eighty percent of people and faster than  eighty percent of people rather than  stronger than ninety percent of people  and slower than fifty what's more is  that these abilities have cross over and  as you improve them you'll see they  naturally reinforce one another as for  why so few people even consider training  their brains as well as their bodies  that's an even bigger mystery to me  brain training would have the most a  direct and immediate impact on our daily  lives our relationships our careers and  even our ability to train efficiently  learning is a form of training and  through brain plasticity we now know  that the brain can grow and change shape  in response to specific training to  tools like meditation and dual n-back  we'll bulk up specific brain networks  just like particular moves will develop  certain muscles in the gym more can be  trained to your reflexes eyesight pretty  much anything you need these things no  less than you need to be able to squat  to 200 kilograms or run an ultra  marathon and in fact as he developed  yourself in every area you give yourself  more options in any situation you become  slightly better at anything to change  your life you need to develop yourself  don't ask what you need to do to get  there ask who you need to become this  kind of total training will make us more  proficient in sports and skills it'll  make us more formidable in a fight it  will provide us with more varied and  versatile abilities it'll make us more  knowledgeable patient and compassionate  will help us see new opportunities and  the sheer process of personal growth  will be endlessly rewarding very  challenging and exciting if you train to  become a better version of yourself to  supplement your general performance and  to complement your lifestyle then surely  it makes sense to bring every facet of  your physical and mental performance up  to the highest possible level in the  given time not just to pick one and call  that training imagine what it would feel  like to be stronger more energetic  smarter more focused more mobile more  alert more resilient more creative more  agile more knowledgeable all at once  imagine what we could become thanks for  watching this guy's I hope you enjoyed  it also I got a new camera not sure if  you noticed but I was kind of loving it  a huge thank you to everyone on patreon  who made that possible and if you want  to get involved and join the Facebook  group you'll find the link in the  description down below likewise if you  enjoy this philosophical whole-brain  body approach  to training then you might enjoy my  ebook and training program super  functional training there's a link in  the description down below and it's on  discount right now whilst we're all  stuck in lockdown or while service are  any ways including yours truly thanks  again for watching team hope you're all  safe and healthy and I'll catch you next  time bye for now  you
 

